From ffda3dfa95c648a0ad0865a675a916e88f04c76c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 12:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Build cell broadcast support without mlite

The cell broadcast controller keeps its settings in dconf via mlite's
MDConfItem, so src/ gained a hard dependency on mlite. mlite is part of the
Nemo stack and is not packaged everywhere, which makes the whole
voicecall-manager unbuildable on those distributions.

Rather than dropping the feature there, put the settings behind
CellBroadcastSettingItem: a typedef for MDConfItem when mlite is available,
and a QSettings-backed stand-in with the same small API when it is not. The
stand-in is per-process instead of system-wide, which is enough because
voicecall-manager owns these keys and everyone else reaches them through its
cell broadcast D-Bus interface.

Also fixes the build with Qt 6 while here: QString::SkipEmptyParts moved to
Qt::SkipEmptyParts in 5.14 and is gone in 6.

Upstream-Status: Pending [written against 8e6ec88, intended for sailfishos/voicecall]
